$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedures for the synthesis of final
products: Protected tripeptide mimetic in MeOH was hydrogenated over 10%
Pd-C (50% by weight of Protected tripeptide mimetic) using a balloon
filled with H2 gas (overnight). The reaction mixture was filtered and
taken to dryness then dissolved in CH2Cl2 to provide a 0.1 M stock
solution of free amine. A liquots of the stock solution were reacted with
appropriate acylating agents in the presence of diisopropylethylamine to
give product. Peptide derivative, pale yellow oil, yield 78%. 1H NMR
(CDCl3) (Present as a mixture of two amide rotamers at the piperidinyl
carboxamide) δ 8.07 (2 H, d, J = 7.81 Hz), 7.94 (2 H, t, J = 8.6 Hz),
7.83 (2 H, m), 7.69 (2 H, m), 7.51-7.42 (7 H, m), 7.39-7.33 (3 H, m),
7.28-7.24 (5 H, m), 7.19-7.13 (11 H, m), 7.01 ( 2 H, m), 6.95 (2 H, m),
6.77 (1 H, s), 6.59 (1 H, s), 5. 76 (1 H, s), 5.71 (1 H, s), 4.64 (1 H,
m), 4.46 (1 H, m), 4.24 (2 H, m), 3.57 (1 H, m), 3.45-3.29 (4 H, m),
3.20-2.77 (11 H, m), 2.67-2.41(11 H, m), 2.33-2.14 (8 H, m), 2.09-1.79
(16 H, m), 1.41-1.33 (54 H, m). FAB-MS (+VE) m/z 1024 (MH+), 1062 (M+K+).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Examination of Acylated 4-Aminopiperidine-4-carboxylic Acid Residues in
the Phosphotyrosyl+1 Position of Grb2 SH2 Domain-Binding Tripeptides
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Kang, Sang-Uk; Choi, Won Jun; Oishi, Shinya; Lee, Kyeong; Karki, Rajeshri
G.; Worthy, Karen M.; Bindu, Lakshman K.; Nicklaus, Marc C.; Fisher,
Robert J.; Burke, Terrence R. Jr.
