$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Peptide 4: Lariat Microcin = GGAGHVPEYFVGIGT-PISFYG. The peptide was
synthesized (0.5 mmol scale) on a PAM resin. To allow on-resin
cyclization between the R-amino and Glu8 γ-carboxyl groups, the
side-chain of Glu8 was orthogonally protected as an allyl ester.
Following chain assembly and Nα deprotection, the allyl group was removed
by treatment with Pd(PPh3)4. The desired lactam linkage was then formed
on the solid phase using PyBOP (5 eq.) as the activating agent and either
DMF or DMSO as the solvent. Cyclization was monitored using the
quantitiative ninhydrin test, which indicated that the coupling
efficiency reached a maximum of ∼50% after three 15 min coupling
procedures. The crude material was purified by RP- HPLC (50-60% D over 60
min.) to give the desired material, peptide 4, (4.5 mg, 2.1 μmole; 2%
yield, based on original loading of the resin). Peptide Synthesis.
General. All peptides were synthesized according to the in-situ
neutralization/HBTU activation protocol for Boc SPPS. Following chain
assembly, global de-protection and cleavage from the support was achieved
by treatment with HF containing 4% v/v p-cresol, for 1 h at 0 °C.
Following removal of the HF, the crude peptide products were precipitated
and washed with anhydrous cold Et2O before being dissolved in aqueous
acetonitrile (50% B) and lyophilized.Peptide 4: Lariat Microcin =
GGAGHVPEYFVGIGT-PISFYG, 2% yield. MS; found m/z 2107.07 ± 0.03, expected
2107.03, and MS2; fragmented with appropriate b and y ions series for
this sequence (Figure 2C). The purified material contained a small amount
of a peptidic contaminant with m/z 2244.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM solid-supported reaction, first reactant attached to PAM resin, DMSO
alternately used as solvent twenty-third stage, other products also
detected
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Structure of Microcin J25, a Peptide Inhibitor of Bacterial RNA
Polymerase, is a Lassoed Tail
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Wilson, Kelly-Anne; Kalkum, Markus; Ottesen, Jennifer; Yuzenkova, Julia;
Chait, Brian T.; Landick, Robert; Muir, Tom; Severinov, Konstantin;
Darst, Seth A.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of the American Chemical Society (2003), 125(41), 12475-12483

$RFMT $RIREG SCHEME189 STEP1
