$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Solid-Phase Synthesis of Peptidomimetic
Scaffold 1. Method A. Fmoc-Rink-amide linker was coupled onto lyophilized
PEGA800 resin via TBTU-activation. The resin was washed with DMF (x6) and
DCM (x5), and then lyophilized overnight. The loading was measured to
0.27 mmol/g. The Fmoc group was removed, and the resin was washed with
DMF (x5). The first amino acid was coupled either as the Pfp ester or via
TBTU-activation, followed by washing with DMF (x5). The Fmoc group was
removed, and the resin was washed with DMF (x5). NaBH3CN (6 equiv) and
glacial acetic acid (18 equiv) were added in DMF, followed by the Fmoc
amino aldehyde (3 equiv). The reaction was monitored, using a Kaiser test
(reaction time usually 3-4 h). The resin was then washed with 96% ethanol
(x3), DCM (x3), and DMF (x5). The Fmoc group was removed, and the resin
was washed with DMF (x5). Fmoc-Cys(SBu t )-OH was then coupled via
TBTUactivation, followed by washing with DMF (x5) and DCM (x5).
Chloroacetic anhydride (25 equiv) and NEM (25 equiv) were added in DCM.
After 30 min, the resin was washed with DMF (x2), DCM (x5), and THF (x2)
and then treated with Bu3P (100 equiv) in THF:saturated sodium acetate
(aqueous) 19:1 for 1 h. The resin was washed with 96% ethanol (x2), DCM
(x5), and DMF (x5), suspended in degassed, dry DMF with NEM (5 equiv),
and then heated to 55-60 °C for 7 h. The resin was washed with DMF (x5).
The Fmoc group was removed, and the resin was washed with DMF (x5).
NaBH3CN (6 equiv), glacial acetic acid (18 equiv), and 1-naphthaldehyde
(3 equiv) were added in DMF. After 20 h, a Kaiser test was negative. The
resin was washed with DMF (x5) and DCM (x5), and the product was cleaved
from the resin by treatment with 95% TFA/TIPS 95:5 (a little DCM was
added to obtain a homogeneous solution) for 2 h. The resin was washed
five times with 95% TFA, three times with glacial acetic acid, and
finally twice with 96% ethanol. The combined washings were concentrated
in vacuo and then lyophilized to give an oil. Diethyl ether was added. An
off-white product was isolated. The crude products 1o and 1p were
purified on preparative HPLC. Method B for R i+2 = Pro. After the
reductive alkylation (performed as in method A), the reduced bond was
capped with Alloc-Cl (5 equiv) and DIPEA (5 equiv) in DCM for 30 min. The
Fmoc group was removed, and the resin was washed with DMF (x5).
Fmoc-Cys(Mmt)-OH was then coupled via HATU-activation, followed by
washing with DMF (x5) and DCM (x5). The Alloc group was subsequently
removed by treatment with (Ph3P)4Pd (3 equiv) under Ar in a degassed
solution of CHCl3/AcOH/NEM 92.5:5:2.5 for 4 h. The resin was washed with
DCM (x5) and DMF (x5). The Fmoc group was removed, and the resin was
washed with DMF (x5). 2-Acetyldimedone (5 equiv) was added in DMF, and
the resin was left overnight or until a Kaiser test was negative (usually
6 h). The reduced bond was then acylated with chloroacetic anhydride (5
equiv) and NEM (5 equiv) in DCM for 30 min. Removal of the Mmt group was
then performed by four successive treatments (10 min each, wash with DCM
between) with DCM:neat TFA:TIPS 90:3:7. The resin was washed with DCM
(x5) and DMF (x5). Cyclization was performed in DMF by addition of DBU (5
equiv). The reaction was monitored using the Ellman test (reaction time
usually 2 h). The resin was washed with DMF (x5), treated with 3%
hydrazine in DMF (3 x 3 min), and washed with DMF (x5). The final
reductive alkylation and subsequent cleavage were performed as in method
A. 1g: Prepared from 200 mg of Fmoc-Rink-PEGA resin. Yield: 1.5 mg (5%).
HPLC purity > 95%. R t (A) = 14.06(96). HRMS (MALDI): exact mass calcd
for C30H34N4O3SNa 553.2244 (MNa+). Found 554.2105 (corresponds to acid).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM solid-supported reaction, first stage is attachment to PEGA800 resin with
Rink amide linker, Rink amide linker used
