$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: To 150 mg (0.57 mmol) of 1-a in 10 mL
N,N-di-methylformamide (DMF) were added 0.04 mL (0.57 mmol) of
cyclopropylamine, 108 mg (0.57 mmol) of
N-(3-dimethylaminopropyl)-N'-ethylcarbodiimide hydrochloride (EDC), and
153 mg (1.1 mmol) of 1-hydroxy-benzotriazole monohydrate (HOBt). The
reaction mixture was stirred at room temperature for two hours. The
solvent was removed in vacuo. To the residue was added saturated aqueous
sodium carbonate, and the product was extracted three times with
dichloro-methane. The combined organic layers were dried over magnesium
sulphate, filtered and concentrated under reduced pressure. The product
was purified by column chromatography using hexane/ethyl acetate (2:1)
mixture as eluent. To 93 mg (0.31mmol) of 1-b in 10 mL methanol wasadded
catalytic amount of palladium on activated carbon. After stirring under
hydrogen gas atmosphere at room temperature for 30 min, the reaction
mixture was filtered with aid of celite. Removal of solvent under reduced
pressure. To 45 mg (0.16 mmol) of 1-c in 10 mL dichloromethane were added
0.013 mL (0.16 mmol) of chloroacetyl chloride and 0.13 mL (0.16 mmol) of
pyridine. The reaction mixture was stirred at room temperature for 6
hours. After removal of solvent under reduced pressure, 10% aqueous
citric acid was added to the residue and the product was extracted three
times with dichloromethane. The combined organic layers were dried over
magnesium sulphate. Removal of solvent in vacuo. Synthesis of
2-Bromo-N-[4-(4-methyl-piperidine-1-yl)-3-(morpholine-4-carbonyl)-phenyl]-acetamide
(12). By the method A, the product was obtained in 1.6% overall yield in
3 steps from 1-a. 1H NMR (CDCl3, 400 MHz): δ 8.19 (s, 1H), 7.64 (dd, J =
6.4,2.4 Hz, 1H), 7.29 (m, 1H), 6.99 (d, J = 8.8 Hz, 1H), 3.97 (s, 1H),
3.94 (m, 1H), 3.81 (m, 1H), 3.66 (m, 2H), 3.64 (m, 1H), 3.54 (m, 1H),
3.48 (m, 2H), 3.09 (m, 2H), 2.85 (t, J = 11.6 Hz, 1H), 2.49 (t, J = 12.8
Hz, 1H), 2.03 (d, J = 7.2 Hz, 2H), 1.77 (m,1H), 1.69 (m, 1H), 1.48 (m,
2H), 0.99 (d, J = 6.8 Hz, 3H).
