$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for solid phase
peptidomimetic synthesis. The synthesis of the four peptidomimetics was
carried out on a Wang resin (0.65 mmol/g) via standard Fmoc strategy and
SPPS protocols 1 Briefly, To a solution of N-Fmoc-Val-OH (10 equiv
relative to resin loading) in dry CH2Cl2 (a few drops of DMF were
required to ensure complete dissolution) under N2 was added
di-iso-propylcarbodiimide (DIC, 5 equiv). The reaction mixture was
stirred for 20 min at 0 °C. In the meantime, the resin was suspended in
dry CH2Cl2 and allowed to swell for 20 min. After filtration, the
symmetrical N-Fmoc-Val anhydride solution and DMAP (0.1 equiv) were added
and the resin was shaken 4 h. After filtration, the resin was
successively washed twice with DMF, MeOH, and CH2Cl2 and again DMF. The
Fmoc protecting group was removed by using twice a solution of piperidine
in DMF (1:4, v/v) for 3 min then for 7 min. After filtration, the resin
was successively washed as before. The SPPS was then continued using
N-Fmoc amino acids (3 equiv) or N-Fmoc-AMBA-OH (3 equiv) in the presence
of HBTU (3 equiv) and DIEA (5 equiv) in DMF. Each coupling reaction was
performed for 45 min, after which time the resin was washed as before.
The last amino acid (i.e., Glu or β-Ala) was introduced as an
N-Boc-protected residue. Completion of each coupling reaction was
monitored via the trinitrobenzenesulfonic acid (TNBS) test. After final
deprotection and cleavage from the resin, all compounds were checked for
purity by RP-HPLC and purified by semipreparative RP-HPLC (see Materials
and Methods). Compound identification was accomplished by ESIMS analysis
in positive mode. Formation of the Resin-Bound Peptidomimetic ELA-1 and
ELA-1.2. To the H-AMBA-L-T-V peptide fragment on Wang resin, N-Aloc-N-(N
'-Fmoc-2-aminoethyl)glycine2 (3 equiv relative to the resin loading) was
introduced using HBTU as coupling reagent (3 equiv) and DIEA (5 equiv).
After classical washings and N-Fmoc removal, the following amino acids
were introduced as described above. The resin-supported Alloc-containing
peptide was then treated at room temperature with Pd(PPh 3) 4 (0.1 equiv)
and PhSiH 3 (20 equiv) in dry CH2Cl2 for 20 min. This deprotection step
was repeated once. Completion of Alloc removal was controlled by using
chloranil test. After filtration, the resin was successively washed twice
with CH2Cl2, MeOH, and again CH2Cl2 . To this resin suspended in CH2Cl2
was added indole acetic acid (5 equiv), HATU (4.5 equiv) and DIEA (7
equiv). The resin was gently shaken overnight, filtered off and washed
following general SPPS procedure. Completion of this acylation step was
checked via chloranil test. Peptides were then released from the resin by
using a TFA/TIS/EDT/H2O (92.5:2.5:2.5:2.5, v/v/v/v) cocktail cleavage to
prevent alkylation of the unprotected indole unit, precipitated using
cold Et2O and then lyophilized. After purification by semi-preparative
RP-HPLC. peptides ELA-1 .7% yields. ELA-1/HLA-A2 ;space group P2 1 ; a (A
°) 58.2 ; b (A °) 84.2 ; c (A °) 84.0 ; β (deg) 90.0 .
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM solid-supported reaction, literature preparation, Fmoc deprotection with
piperidine/DMF, attachment to Wang resin in stage 2, process repeated
twice in stage 9
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Crystal Structures of HLA-A*0201 Complexed with Melan-A/MART-126(27)-35
Peptidomimetics Reveal Conformational Heterogeneity and Highlight
Degeneracy of T Cell Recognition
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Douat-Casassus, Celine; Borbulevych, Oleg; Tarbe, Marion; Gervois,
Nadine; Jotereau, Francine; Baker, Brian M.; Quideau, Stephane
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Medicinal Chemistry (2010), 53(19), 7061-7066

