$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General method of solid phase peptide synthesis. Fmoc protecting groups
were removed by treatment with 20% piperidine in DMF for 15 min, followed
by three washes with DMF. A 0.5 M solution of N-Fmoc-protected amino acid
(10 eq.), HOBt (10 eq.) in DMF and sequentially DIC (10 eq.) were added
to the resin. The resin was shaken overnight. For each following step of
the solid phase peptide synthesis, the same deprotection and coupling
reactions were performed, but for each subsequent amino acid coupling, 3
equivalents of each reagent were used. Capping of N-terminal amine was
achieved by shaking the resin with a 0.5 M solution of acetic anhydride
(10 eq.) and DIEA (15 eq.) in DMF for 15 min. Removal of Alloc protecting
group. The whole procedure of Alloc deprotection was conducted under a
positive flow of argon. The resin was solvated with CH2Cl2 for 5 min. The
solvent was drained, and PhSiH3 (24 eq.) in CH2Cl2 was added to the resin
followed by Pd(pph3)4 (0.25 eq.) in CH2Cl2. After agitating the resin for
1 h by bubbling with argon, the solution was drained, and the resin was
washed with CH2Cl2 (3x). General method for synthesis of Aza-peptide
epoxides. A 0.4 M solution of ethyl L-trans-epoxysuccinic acid (10 eq.)
and HOBt (10 eq.) in DMF and sequentially DIC (10 eq.) were added to the
resin. After shaking overnight, the solution was drained, the resin was
washed with DMF followed by CH2Cl2, dried in vacuo, and subjected to
cleavage and purification. Z-EVaD-epoxide (1): Synthesized according to
the above described general protocol. 26% yield. ESI-MS: 595.4 [M+H]+ 1H
NMR (500 MHz, CD3CN/CD3OD): δ 7.49-7.40 (m, 5H), 5.20-5.13 (m, 2H),
4.32-4.19 (m, 4H), 4.05 (bs, 1H), 3.60 (bs, 1H), 2.44 (t, 2H, J = 7.4
Hz), 2.18-2.02 (m, 3H), 1.96-1.90 (m, 1H), 1.32 (t, 3H, J = 7.2 Hz), 0.98
(d, 6H, J = 3.7 Hz). HRMS: found [M+Na]+ 617.2108. C26H34N4NaO12 +
requires 617.2071.
