$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Boc-Ala-Gly-Pro-Ile-NHBn 26. Compound 25 (347
mg, 0.8 mmol) was vigorously stirred with 10% Pd-C (50 mg) in methanol
(40 mL) under 4 bars of hydrogen for 1 hr at room temperature. The
catalyst was removed by filtration, washed with methanol and DCM and the
filtrate was evaporated under reduced pressure. A mixture of the crude
product and isoleucine benzylamide trifluoroacetic salt (132 mg, 0.8
mmol) was treated with DIEA (418 μL, 3 equiv.), HOBT (123 mg, 0.8 mmol)
and DCC (183 mg, 0.88 mmol) in DCM (20 mL) overnight at room temperature.
The reaction was quenched by addition of several drops of acetic acid and
the precipitate was removed by filtration. The filtrate was evaporated to
dryness and the crude product was purified by silica gel flash
chromatography (chloroform:methanol 95:5) without prior workup. 26.
Boc-Gly-Pro-Ile-OMe 33 Purification by silica gel flash chromatography
(eluent: ethyl acetate:hexane 90:10) afforded 33: (1.08 g, 90%). 1H NMR
(CDCl3): δ 7.19 (d, 1H, J = 8.1), 5.42 (bs, 1H), 4.60 (m, 1H), 4.48 (dd,
1H, J = 4.8, J= 8.3), 3.94 (m, 2H), 3.73 (s, 3H), 3.73-3.38 (m, 2H), 2.34
(m, 1H), 2.03 (m, 2H), 1.88 (m, 2H), 1.45 (s, 9H), 1.36 (m, 2H), 1.10 (m,
2H), 0.88 (m, 6H); 13C NMR (CDCl3): δ 172.2, 170.5, 168.6, 155.8, 79.8,
60.0, 56.8, 52.1, 46.3, 43.1, 37.6, 28.33, 27.3, 25.1, 24.9, 15.5, 11.6.
