$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM The above dried resin was swollen in CHCl3 and treated with [PPh3]4Pd(0)
(0.16 g, 0.14 mmol) in CHCl3/AcOH/NEM (37:2:1)for 1.5 h under N2. The
resin was washed with DCM, THF, and DMF. To this resin was added 3 mL of
DMF solution containing HATU (41 mg, 0.11 mmol), HOAt (15 mg, 0.11 mmol),
NEM (14μL, 0.11 mmol), and H-Pro-O-allyl (84 mg, 0.54 mmol), and the
mixture was stirred overnight at 25 °C. The mixture was filtered,and the
resin was washed with DMF and ether and dried to yield 5. The C-terminal
allyl and N-terminal Fmoc groups were then removed as described above.
The product resin (50 mg) was treated with TFA/H2O (95:5, 1 mL) for 1 h
at 25 °C. After evaporation of the TFA, ether was added, and the
resulting precipitate was purified with semipreparative HPLC to yield a
homogeneous product (yield 20%) showing a single peak on ananalytical
HPLC compound 6, yield 20% HPLC tR, 11.74 min (CH3CN, 10-40%/30 min,
Figure 4); MALDI-TOFMS m/z 747.79 for [M + H]+ (calcd 747.89 for
C36H59N8O9).Isomer: HPLC tR, 12.91 min (CH3CN, 10-40%/30 min, Figure4);
MALDI-TOF MS m/z 747.46 for [M + H]+ (calcd 747.89 for C36H59N8O9).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM combinatorial, solid-supported reaction, first stage is attachment to
CLEAR resin, in-situ generated reactant from stage 11 added to crude from
stage 10 in stage 12 stereoselective Horner-Emmons reaction (key step),
other product also detected
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Solid-Phase Syntheses of Olefin-Containing Inhibitors for HTLV-1 Protease
Using the Horner-Emmons Reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Bang, Jeong Kyu; Naka, Hiromi; Teruya, Kenta; Aimoto, Saburo; Konno,
Hiroyuki; Nosaka, Kazuto; Tatsumi, Tadashi; Akaji, Kenichi
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Organic Chemistry (2005), 70(25), 10596-10599

$RFMT $RIREG SCHEME326 STEP1
$RXN



