$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 4N HCl in 1,4-dioxane (1 mL) was added to a solution of 9 (290 mg, 0.46
mmol) in MeOH (10 mL). The mixture was stirred at room temperature
overnight and then concentrated to give an ammonium salt.
L-N-t-Boc-N-methyl-alanine (110 mg, 0.54 mmol), EDC (106 mg, 0.55 mmol),
HOBt (74 mg, 0.55 mmol) and N,Ndiisopropylethylamine (1 mL) were added to
a mixture of this salt in CH2Cl2 (15 mL). The mixture was stirred at room
temperature overnight and concentrated then the residue was purified by
chromatography to afford an amide. Pd-C (10%, 50 mg) was added to a
solution of this amide in MeOH and the mixture was stirred under 1 atm of
H2 overnight and then filtered through celite to remove the catalyst. The
filtration was concentrated to give compound 10 (204 mg, 77% over three
steps) compound 10 , yield (204 mg, 77% over three steps) 1HNMR (300 MHz,
CDCl3, TMS) δ 7.32-7.18 (m, 11H), 6.90 (brs, 1H), 6.22 (d, J = 7.3 Hz,
1H), 5.05 (m, 1H), 4.70 (t, J = 8.5 Hz, 1H), 4.50 (brm, 1H), 4.25 (m,
1H), 2.99 (m, 1H), 2.83 (m, 1H), 2.81 (s, 3H), 2.65 (m, 1H), 2.45 (m,
1H), 2.28 (t, J = 11 Hz, 1H), 2.18-2.05 (m, 2H), 1.80-1.65 (m, 2H), 1.53
(s, 9H), 1.45 (m, 1H), 1.30 (d, J = 7.1 Hz, 3H); ESI MS: m/z 600.4
(M+Na)+.
